,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kunigami language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunigami_language,"Kunigami, also known as Northern Okinawan or Yanbaru (山原言葉, ヤンバルクトゥーバ, Yanbaru Kutūba) is a Ryukyuan language of northern Okinawa Island in Kunigami District and the city of Nago, otherwise known as the Yanbaru region and historically encompassing the territory of the kingdom of Hokuzan.",Kunigami,Japonic
1,Okinoerabu dialect cluster - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okinoerabu_dialect_cluster,"The Okinoerabu dialect cluster (島ムニ Shimamuni), also Oki-no-Erabu, is a dialect cluster spoken on Okinoerabu Island, Kagoshima Prefecture of southwestern Japan. It is part of the Amami-Okinawan languages, which are part of the Japonic languages.",Kunigami,Japonic
